WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.496
Stopping conditions: you need more than one.

2
00:00:02.776 --> 00:00:09.133
A loop that ends only when the model stops calling tools is fine for a demo and dangerous in production.

3
00:00:09.413 --> 00:00:11.035
Plan for four kinds of stop.

4
00:00:11.315 --> 00:00:12.445
Natural stop.

5
00:00:12.725 --> 00:00:18.869
The model returns a response with no tool calls (on the Claude API, stop_reason is end_turn ).

6
00:00:19.149 --> 00:00:28.216
Treat this as a claim of completion and verify it where you can: run the tests, check that every record was handled, confirm the answer cites a source.

7
00:00:28.496 --> 00:00:30.075
Abnormal stop reasons.

8
00:00:30.355 --> 00:00:35.624
max_tokens can cut a tool call off mid-input, and refusal means the model declined.

9
00:00:35.904 --> 00:00:37.248
Neither should run tools.

10
00:00:37.528 --> 00:00:42.115
pause_turn means a server tool paused and the request should be resent as is.

11
00:00:42.395 --> 00:00:43.376
Hard limits.

12
00:00:43.656 --> 00:00:46.173
Cap the number of model calls, and cap spend.

13
00:00:46.453 --> 00:01:07.573
Every framework has the first: the Claude SDK tool runner takes max_iterations, the Claude Agent SDK takes max_turns and max_budget_usd, the OpenAI Agents SDK takes max_turns and raises MaxTurnsExceeded, and smolagents runs until a final answer or its maximum number of steps.

14
00:01:07.853 --> 00:01:14.424
Defaults differ, and the Agent SDK documents no limit on either by default, so set them yourself.

15
00:01:14.704 --> 00:01:21.232
Note how the Agent SDK counts: each turn with tool calls, plus one for the final text answer.

16
00:01:21.512 --> 00:01:22.792
No-progress stops.

17
00:01:23.072 --> 00:01:27.509
The agent repeats the same call, or several steps add no new information.

18
00:01:27.789 --> 00:01:40.547
A budget will eventually catch this, but detecting it earlier saves money and gives a better error message: “stopped after three identical searches” tells the person reading the trace exactly what went wrong.

19
00:01:40.827 --> 00:01:46.416
When a hard limit trips, end gracefully: return what you have, mark it as partial, and record why.

20
00:01:46.696 --> 00:02:00.776
The Agent SDK does this with result subtypes such as error_max_turns and error_max_budget_usd, and its docs warn that spend can pass the dollar cap by up to the cost of the response that crossed it, so leave headroom.
